## [=step]. Permission (required: the application refuses to start without it)

`backend/src/main/java/com/admintemplate/security/Permissions.java`, with the other constants:

```java
    /** Create, change and delete [=module.name] data (SpecForge module). */
    public static final String [=module.permissionConstant] = "[=module.permission]";
```

and at the end of `ALL`:

```java
            SETTINGS_ADMIN, AUDIT_VIEW, [=module.permissionConstant]);
```

and in `Authorize.java` (`PermissionsTest` checks that every permission has one):

```java
    public static final String [=module.permissionConstant] = HAS + Permissions.[=module.permissionConstant] + END;
```

<#if module.frontend>
and in `frontend/apps/web/src/lib/auth/permissions.ts`, at the end of the `Permission` type:

```ts
  | '[=module.permission]'
```

</#if>
The generated controllers use the same expression as a literal, `"hasAuthority('[=module.permission]')"`, so they
compile before these lines exist.
</#if>
<#assign step = step + 1>

